Derive the following Enthalpy and Constant-Pressure Processes relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or thermodynamic identity used at each step.
\[
\begin{aligned}
dH&=dU+p\,dV+V\,dp\\
&=T\,dS+V\,dp.
\end{aligned}
\tag*{[2]}
\]
Notation: \(H,U\) denotes enthalpy and internal energy; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(H_m,\Delta H_m\) denotes molar enthalpy and its finite change; unit \(\mathrm{J mol^{-1}, J mol^{-1}}\); \(T_1,T_2,p,V,S\) denotes initial and final temperature, pressure, total volume, and entropy; unit \(\mathrm{K, K, Pa, m^{3}, J K^{-1}}\); \(p_{\mathrm{ext}}\) denotes external pressure; unit \(\mathrm{Pa}\); \(Q_p,\delta Q\) denotes finite heat and infinitesimal heat transferred into the system; unit \(\mathrm{J, J}\); \(n,C_P\) denotes amount and molar heat capacity at constant pressure; unit \(\mathrm{mol, J mol^{-1} K^{-1}}\); \(a,b,c\) denotes coefficients in the molar heat-capacity model; unit \(\mathrm{J mol^{-1} K^{-1}, J mol^{-1} K^{-2}, J K mol^{-1}}\).

